<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:24:48Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Israel: Eisenkot officially tasked with forming a government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01e374bce7f46d540995bf9115e9f6cb9c901e8d4700cb96c7c9e250a4b6eb0e</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:24:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israel-eisenkot-officially-tasked-with-forming-a-government/a-79891422--47e8dba46615.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israel-eisenkot-officially-tasked-with-forming-a-government/a-79891422?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Israeli President Isaac Herzog tasked Gadi Eisenkot with the right of trying to form a government. The opposition leader's way to replacing Benjamin Netanyahu as prime minister is full of political challenges.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>At least 21 killed after migrant boat sinks off Senegal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1fdc576d7293d31e562fb018b2e45ded45207cab53cae88912f63ec22aa8c665</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:24:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T13:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/at-least-21-killed-after-migrant-boat-sinks-off-senegal/a-79890883--85de81bd8398.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/at-least-21-killed-after-migrant-boat-sinks-off-senegal/a-79890883?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The incident occurred near Kebemer off the coast of northwestern Senegal. Authorities on El Hierro in the Canary Islands have declared an emergency after a marked increase in migrant boat arrivals.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran: US strikes ship after Hormuz blockade breach</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b26de3d73cd2ea326ddd4a8dc4f3f423c4f3c8e7ac1423b2cbd16842c1b40844</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:24:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T13:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-us-strikes-ship-after-hormuz-blockade-breach/a-79890434--13b5e59a0bc3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-us-strikes-ship-after-hormuz-blockade-breach/a-79890434?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US military said a vessel trying to leave an Iranian port was hit due to the naval blockade on the country. On its part, Iran said three "non compliant" oil tankers caught fire in the Strait of Hormuz.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Gaza: Rains add misery to humanitarian catastrophe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a1b1e108a09fe4fa7562590ad7d5c5959add1c09fef5879e4d2a4a7a579b005</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:24:30Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T10:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gaza-rains-add-misery-to-humanitarian-catastrophe/a-79889580--aadff38d36aa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gaza-rains-add-misery-to-humanitarian-catastrophe/a-79889580?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With most homes damaged or destroyed by the war, Gazans are facing worsening humanitarian conditions due to heavy rain.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'Never Again!': Holocaust remembrance under pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79ea61860e9e8ea9db7ffb2f32d19d725a393df96a91541f5e6af2423081a00f</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:24:33Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T09:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/never-again-holocaust-remembrance-under-pressure/a-79840894--861f4756e8c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/never-again-holocaust-remembrance-under-pressure/a-79840894?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Only a few Holocaust survivors remain who can share their stories firsthand. Meanwhile, voices calling for an end to what they describe as a "cult of guilt" are growing louder. How can Holocaust remembrance survive?</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Poland begins two days of mourning over Krakow shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbbd387a71139fbaf2a9ab06f3119352414a14c4156a687c6da6080f2c1da4d6</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:24:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T09:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/poland-begins-two-days-of-mourning-over-krakow-shooting/a-79889400--0eccdd37b487.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/poland-begins-two-days-of-mourning-over-krakow-shooting/a-79889400?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Polish authorities have opened a terror probe after the shooting on Krakow's Main Square. Police confirmed that the bodies found at the suspect's home were those of his parents and sister.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Friedrich Merz set to confirm presidential nominee</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7cee3484d29cceb84b6903bd9b1a1592759e64570c86eba4a4c48fbc3e62a4ad</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:24:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T09:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-friedrich-merz-set-to-confirm-presidential-nominee/live-79883533--112a84f4b735.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-friedrich-merz-set-to-confirm-presidential-nominee/live-79883533?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The executive committee of the German chancellor's CDU party is expected to finalize its nomination for the country's president. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India: Delhi chokes on most polluted Diwali eve in 10 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb65fc8d976252317a0142962924074d7df84f2a616576c9d0f173e0d826ea74</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:24:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T07:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-delhi-chokes-on-most-polluted-diwali-eve-in-10-years/live-79883248--b4ed1b7f6c06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-delhi-chokes-on-most-polluted-diwali-eve-in-10-years/live-79883248?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Delhi was ranked as the world's most polluted major city on the eve of Diwali. Delhi's air pollution is expected to get worse in the coming days. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>As COP31 Antalya kicks off, can world move beyond big promises?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:519430a953716ed979bfb04046be32b07488259232d14f75bb474a5a819d48f5</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T05:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-cop31-antalya-kicks-off-can-world-move-beyond-big-promises/a-79661366--3ff0bee69cef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-cop31-antalya-kicks-off-can-world-move-beyond-big-promises/a-79661366?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Droughts, floods and extreme heat are upping the pressure on delegates at the UN climate talks in Antalya, Turkey. Can countries move beyond pledges to concrete action?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Poland: Gunman kills 6 in Krakow main square, police say</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:476b1e1d0eddf3f3d0f02ee39f4ab2f4fc0958f47b12c2ebac023b08a8be6f88</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:24:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T21:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/poland-gunman-kills-6-in-krakow-main-square/a-79886489--2e26ae8c4338.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/poland-gunman-kills-6-in-krakow-main-square-police-say/a-79886489?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A suspect who fired from a car killed at least six people, including a British tourist, in Krakow's main market square. Officials said the man was fascinated with "radical" and "far-right" ideologies.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ebola: Why is there still no vaccine?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:59476f09b8aa478ba7519bcf4f5dea5f6037071fadb3c826521bb99cf4b42f0c</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T21:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ebola-why-is-there-still-no-vaccine/a-79888134--134cc892a91f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ebola-why-is-there-still-no-vaccine/a-79888134?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ebola has been known about for decades, but there is still no vaccine against the Bundibugyo strain of the virus causing the current outbreak. New research raises hopes of protection against the various types of Ebola.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli president tasks Gadi Eisenkot with forming government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:59ee9196c37c69bed1627aa8bfb5d97f2e479b28683ec11989c3c25b2c9a880d</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T19:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israeli-president-tasks-gadi-eisenkot-with-forming-government/a-79888288--1dfc2b75eb80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israeli-president-tasks-gadi-eisenkot-with-forming-government/a-79888288?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">President Isaac Herzog has picked former Israeli military chief Gadi Eisenkot, leader of an anti-Netanyahu alliance, to take the first shot at trying to form a government. Tricky coalition talks are expected.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Trump offers White House press secretary role to Dana White</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7eb5fe07e9a4f810e1e1ed7512cd584e0d15a93f05d999ab460d5c9fc6ff9e11</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T19:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-offers-white-house-press-secretary-role-to-dana-white/a-79888119--34dff2f985d0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-offers-white-house-press-secretary-role-to-dana-white/a-79888119?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump has offered the White House press secretary job to Dana White, the chief executive of the Ultimate Fighting Championship. White has neither formally accepted nor turned down the invitation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France sees new round of Yellow Vest, student protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:46e4d8e50bf4b518883cc64b3587d4698906832113e5efc9fa4c1b654a05e162</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T19:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-sees-new-round-of-yellow-vest-student-protests/a-79884064--3a9e4c3fcc71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-sees-new-round-of-yellow-vest-student-protests/a-79884064?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Although fewer protesters turned out in comparison with previous weeks, several cities saw clashes between police and demonstrators.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Armenia's selective prosecution: A threat to EU relations?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ad3f60ef4cac2794a565b08e46884c79cc5fde01c99806741ce50d6865a0b379</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T18:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/armenia-s-selective-prosecution-a-threat-to-eu-relations/a-79878159--345ae9a3ae32.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/armenia-s-selective-prosecution-a-threat-to-eu-relations/a-79878159?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While Brussels has refrained from harsh criticism, Armenian civil society has warned of selective justice against opposition figures. Could the EU's pragmatic stance risk repeating past mistakes?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Africa's ANC facing worst-ever performance in local elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf4bf1c5a15f3e9cf19c4f0d02fc651144a46d5e8c004e89dc36258b4aaf2ea4</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T18:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-africa-s-anc-facing-worst-ever-performance-in-local-elections/a-79887482--0f01de17e4d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-africa-s-anc-facing-worst-ever-performance-in-local-elections/a-79887482?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Near-final results show South Africa's once dominant ANC will see its lowest-ever vote percentage. The party is taking the blame for shoddy municipal services, including water and electricity shortages.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>More than 40,000 gather as Pope Leo XIV celebrates Mass in Uruguay</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1c15dc8f68bdba93091444c1e4e3abc6618e6f158451813cb0229c6ca99791f</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T16:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/more-than-40-000-gather-as-pope-leo-xiv-celebrates-mass-in-uruguay/a-79886543--b939280d1b50.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/more-than-40-000-gather-as-pope-leo-xiv-celebrates-mass-in-uruguay/a-79886543?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Leo celebrated the first Mass of his South America tour less than a month after undergoing cancer surgery. He is seeking to raise interest in the Catholic Church in Uruguay, South America's most secular country.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Should AI companies pay for the journalism they use?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f5e7a71384bf27f9872f088b36b5d0a1de289f577ca9cc80e67e6e6ad3abf6b7</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:24:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T15:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/should-ai-companies-pay-for-the-journalism-they-use/a-79884854--921e36bf95d6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/should-ai-companies-pay-for-the-journalism-they-use/a-79884854?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Publishers say AI chatbots are using their reporting to answer readers' questions while sending back less traffic and less money. Should the companies that build these tools pay for the journalism they rely on?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Son of Iran's shah receives 'Freedom Prize' in Frankfurt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fdd49af2083552953c8082fccca992d8646cf04dd39910e4fe6be2e349bd5de7</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T14:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/son-of-iran-s-shah-receives-freedom-prize-in-frankfurt/a-79885661--aa99dccac573.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/son-of-iran-s-shah-receives-freedom-prize-in-frankfurt/a-79885661?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">18,000 people gathered in Frankfurt to show support for Reza Pahlavi, the son of the Iranian monarch ousted in 1979. Factions in the opposition have accused him of not distancing himself from his father's rule.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>After victory in the midterms, what next for US Democrats?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2209502b338156d5176d57bb627a78ff0031d7f758f083d839b52af50012fe1c</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T14:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-victory-in-the-midterms-what-next-for-us-democrats/a-79884957--f8ad14f3dbbf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-victory-in-the-midterms-what-next-for-us-democrats/a-79884957?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's Republican party has lost its majority in both chambers of the US Congress. But the president still has a lot of power — and the Democrats have yet to agree on how best to use theirs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Italy's Meloni blames pro-Russian hackers for cyberattack on minister</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cfd7d1bbf9d652acfe23475163e79ba6c235380fdb2c7f1ab6e3f92f9d66c89e</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T14:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/italy-s-meloni-blames-pro-russian-hackers-for-cyberattack-on-minister/a-79885200--f6543501c58b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/italy-s-meloni-blames-pro-russian-hackers-for-cyberattack-on-minister/a-79885200?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Antonio Tajani has said hackers published personal data stolen from him as Giorgia Meloni blamed pro-Russia criminals for the incident. The news follows a string of bomb threats that have grounded flights across the EU.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
